Experiment 1 – Student Event Registration Form
Aim
To create a simple event registration form using HTML.
Step 1: Create a folder
Open Command Prompt or Git Bash and type:
mkdir RegistrationForm
cd RegistrationForm
Step 2: Create the HTML file
In Windows Command Prompt:
notepad registration.html
In Git Bash / Ubuntu:
nano registration.html
Step 3: Write this complete code
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Event Registration Form</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h2>Event Registration Form</h2>

    <form>
        <label>Full Name:</label>
        <input type="text" name="name" required>
        <br><br>

        <label>Email:</label>
        <input type="email" name="email" required>
        <br><br>

        <label>Phone Number:</label>
        <input type="tel" name="phone" required>
        <br><br>

        <label>Gender:</label>
        <input type="radio" name="gender" value="Male"> Male
        <input type="radio" name="gender" value="Female"> Female
        <br><br>

        <label>Department:</label>
        <select name="department">
            <option>CSE</option>
            <option>IT</option>
            <option>ECE</option>
            <option>EEE</option>
            <option>MECH</option>
        </select>
        <br><br>

        <label>Event:</label>
        <select name="event">
            <option>Technical</option>
            <option>Cultural</option>
            <option>Sports</option>
        </select>
        <br><br>

        <input type="submit" value="Register">
        <input type="reset" value="Clear">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
Save the file.
Step 4: Run and view the form
Open the RegistrationForm folder and double-click registration.html. It opens in a web browser. Enter details and click Register.
Expected result: The Student Event Registration Form appears in the browser with name, email, phone, gender, department, event, Register and Clear fields.
Note: This is a basic HTML form. It displays the form and performs browser-side required-field checks; it does not save registrations to a database.
Result
The event registration form was created successfully using HTML.
Viva Questions
What is HTML? HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It is used to create web pages.
What is a form? A form collects information from users.
What is the use of <form>? It defines an HTML form.
What is the use of <input>? It creates input fields.
What is the use of type="radio"? It allows the user to select one option from a group.
What is the use of <select>? It creates a drop-down list.
What is the use of required? It makes a field compulsory.
What is the use of submit? It submits the form.
Experiment 8 – Create a Code Snippets Library Using GitHub
Aim
To create a GitHub repository and upload sample code files using Git commands.
Step 1: Create a repository on GitHub
Open https://github.com and sign in.
Click New repository.
Enter repository name: Code-Snippets-Library.
Select Public.
Click Create repository.
Step 2: Clone the repository
Open Git Bash or Ubuntu Terminal. Replace USERNAME with your GitHub username.
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/Code-Snippets-Library.git
cd Code-Snippets-Library
Step 3: Create the Python file
nano hello.py
Write:
print("Hello World")
print("Welcome to Code Snippets Library")
Save in nano: press Ctrl + O, press Enter, then Ctrl + X.
Step 4: Create the Java file
nano Hello.java
Write:
class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello World");
        System.out.println("Java Code Snippet");
    }
}
Save and exit nano.
Step 5: Create the HTML file
nano index.html
Write:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Code Snippets</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h2>Hello World</h2>
    <p>Welcome to Code Snippets Library</p>
</body>
</html>
Save and exit nano.
Step 6: Create README file
nano README.md
Write:
# Code Snippets Library

This repository contains simple code examples.

## Files
- hello.py – Python Hello World program
- Hello.java – Java Hello World program
- index.html – Basic HTML page
Save and exit nano.
Step 7: Add, commit and push files
Run these commands from inside the Code-Snippets-Library folder:
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Added code snippets"
git push origin main
If your repository's branch is named master, use:
git push origin master
Step 8: Verify
Refresh your GitHub repository page. You should see:
hello.py
Hello.java
index.html
README.md
Result
A Code Snippets Library repository was created and the sample code files were uploaded to GitHub using Git.
Viva Questions
What is Git? Git is a version control system used to track changes in files.
What is GitHub? GitHub is an online platform for hosting Git repositories.
What is a repository? A repository is a place where project files and their history are stored.
What does git clone do? It copies a remote repository to the local computer.
What does git add . do? It stages all changes in the current folder.
What does git commit do? It saves the staged changes in the local repository.
What does git push do? It uploads local commits to the remote repository.
What is README.md? It is a Markdown file that explains the project.
What is the difference between Git and GitHub? Git is the version control tool; GitHub hosts Git repositories online.
Important command reminder
For the registration form, create and edit registration.html, then open it in a browser.
For the code snippets library, type Git commands in Git Bash or Ubuntu Terminal, not inside the HTML/Python/Java files.
Replace USERNAME in the clone URL with your actual GitHub username.
